.TH CMP 1 
.SH NAME
cmp \- compare two files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmp
[
.B \-lsL
]
.I file1 file2
[
.I offset1
[
.I offset2
]
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The two files are
compared.
A diagnostic results if the contents differ, otherwise
there is no output.
By default,
.B cmp
prints the byte number of the first differing byte.
.PP
The options are:
.TP
.B -l
Print the byte number (decimal) and the
differing bytes (hexadecimal) for each difference.
.TP
.B -s
Print nothing for differing files,
but set the exit status.
.TP
.B -L
Print the line number of the first differing byte.
.PP
If offsets are given,
comparison starts at the designated byte position
of the corresponding file.
Offsets use a decimal prefix, as in the original Limbo command.
A leading sign and whitespace are accepted; trailing text is ignored.
Comparison byte and line numbers start at one after the offsets.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/cmp.zi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IR diff (1) 
